; LCNC-SUITE ORIGINAL — not vendored from upstream.
;
; Plane-mode touch-off: set the WORKPIECE datum (G54) from a point touched in
; the tilted plane. Called by the gateway's `touchoff` command when the Plane
; jog frame is active (kins 2, G59):
;
;     o<twp_touchoff> call [mask] [x] [y] [z]
;
; mask bits: 1 = X given, 2 = Y given, 4 = Z given (values for unset bits are
; ignored). Semantics per axis are G10 L20's — "make the current position
; read v" — in the plane frame the DRO shows. The datum is then written where
; it lives: remap.py twp_touchoff maps the new plane-frame origin back through
; the head solve (the frame the kins pins hold) and the LIVE table pose into
; the table frame, subtracts the plane's own origin vector, and writes G54;
; G59..G59.3 are rewritten to match, so the DRO reads v at once and the next
; Orient recomputes the same rows from G54 (the round trip the live check
; pins). Nothing moves.
;
; The leading M66 is what makes the interpreter's current position CURRENT
; (queue drained, read-ahead stopped) — the same reliance twp_reorient.ngc
; places on it before M530. IJK carry the values: an M-code line cannot
; carry X/Y/Z words (see g533remap.ngc).
o<twp_touchoff>sub
(WEBUI_SUB=twp_touchoff) ;lcnc-suite: preview sub-span marker, silent in task

M66 L0 E0                                  ;force sync, stop read ahead
M535 P#1 I#2 J#3 K#4
M66 L0 E0

(WEBUI_SUB_END) ;lcnc-suite: preview sub-span marker
o<twp_touchoff>endsub
m2
